/// RAKHAL-276 (v2 correction): was ACTIVE|COMPLETED. `COMPLETED` is renamed
/// `RELEASED` and is now reached *only* via `HealthService.releaseWithdrawal`
/// (an explicit, audited action) — never as a side effect of a read. The new
/// `READY_FOR_RELEASE` value is the state a withdrawal sits in once its
/// `until` date has passed but nobody has confirmed release yet; the daily
/// sweep cron (`SchedulerService.runDailySweeps`) is the only place that
/// transitions ACTIVE -> READY_FOR_RELEASE. `CANCELLED` covers a withdrawal
/// voided before its window elapsed (e.g. logged in error).
///
/// Migration note: the Postgres enum type keeps the legacy `COMPLETED` value
/// (Postgres can't cheaply drop enum values without a rename/recreate, and
/// this ticket's migration is deliberately additive-only) — `COMPLETED` is
/// simply never written or read by application code from this point on.
enum SafetyWithdrawalStatus {
  ACTIVE
  READY_FOR_RELEASE
  RELEASED
  CANCELLED
}

enum HealthCloseOutcome {
  RECOVERED
  MORTALITY
}

/// RAKHAL-275: structured condition classification, kept alongside the
/// free-text `diagnosis` field (nullable/additive — diagnosis remains the
/// source of detail, condition is a coarse structured bucket for reporting).
